@voice haddad-tamsin
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Tamsin Haddad: galley hand, early team, Bunk 6 berth 2. Off Wednesday and
// Thursday. Roster: optimistic, nervous; evening-shower, lingers-at-meals. Knows every song in the record cabinet (one
// of five who say so, none agreeing); learning the guitar, badly (from the same battered book as Hamid, Noor Park and
// Isak Lindqvist). Pronouns: she / her (facts.md 4b).
//
// HOW SHE TALKS: bright, quick to say it'll all be fine, then a small "won't it?" on the end. Sings under her breath
// and stops when noticed. Apologises for things that aren't her fault.
// WITH JUNIORS: delighted to help; slightly too much.
// WHAT SHE NOTICES: the radio; the words to anything; anyone left out.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = sings out loud. Nervous = "It'll be fine!" twice. Low = lingers at the table long after the meal.
// NEVER: unkind; sure of herself for long.
// RUNNING: today is always the day the chord comes right; the lyrics war; guitar practice with Hamid, which helps neither.
tpl: warm
talk: Bright, quick to say it'll be fine, then "won't it?"; sings under her breath and stops when noticed; apologises too much.
